course: dictionary
lesson: 4227
title: The gram: measuring small weights
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gram is a small unit for measuring how heavy something is. Scientists call this its mass. A paper clip weighs about one gram, so a gram is a useful size for light things. «The bee hummingbird from Cuba weighs about two grams.» That tells you the bird is very light, about as heavy as two paper clips.
explain: Grams also help you read the world around you. «A kilogram is 1000 grams», so a kilogram is a much bigger weight. «A litre is 1000 millilitres.» Each unit is a thousand times bigger than the one before it. When you see a number with g after it, like 250 g, it means 250 grams.
explain: Food labels use grams to show how much sugar and fat is in a packet. Shops also use grams to compare prices fairly. «The unit price is the price for one gram, one litre, or one item.» So a big pack and a small pack can be compared by price per gram, not just by the price on the front.
fact: A gram is a unit of weight, or mass, used for small things.
fact: One gram is about the weight of a paper clip.
fact: 1000 grams make 1 kilogram.
fact: A milligram is one thousandth of a gram.
fact: The short form for gram is g, as in 250 g.
fact: «Gramme» is an older British spelling of gram that you may still see.
exercise: «The bee hummingbird from Cuba weighs about two grams.» What does gram measure here? | *How heavy something is | How hot something gets | How long something lasts | How far something travels
exercise: «A kilogram is 1000 grams.» How many grams make one kilogram? | 10000 | *1000 | 100 | 10
exercise: Ella reads «250 g» on a packet of crisps. What does the g stand for? | *Gram | Gold | Glass | Gross
test: «The elf owl weighs about 40 grams, about as much as a sparrow.» Which answer gives the right way to say how heavy the owl is? | *40 grams | 40 litres | 40 metres | 40 years
test: A milligram is one thousandth of a gram. How many milligrams are in one gram? | *1000 | 1 | 100 | 10
exam: «The unit price is the price for one gram.» Mia wants to compare two packs of rice that are different sizes fairly. What should she compare? | The biggest picture on the front | The colour of the packets | *The price per gram of each pack | Which pack is closer to the till
